# What never enters the build context.
#
# Two jobs, and the first one is the important one: `.env` holds
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, and a build context that contains it is one `COPY . .`
# away from a secret baked into a layer that `docker history` will happily
# print. PLAN.md §11 passes the variables in at *run* time with --env-file, so
# the file has no business being here at all. `backend/tests/test_packaging.py`
# asserts this pattern is present, because the failure is silent.
#
# The second job is size and cache churn: node_modules is ~500 MB of files the
# builder stage reinstalls from the lockfile anyway, and a stale frontend/out
# would be uploaded only to be overwritten by `npm run build`.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.mutation-worktree
.playwright-mcp

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node
**/node_modules
frontend/out
frontend/.next
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime state — the database lives in a volume, never in the image
db/*.db
db/*.db-wal
db/*.db-shm

# Not needed to build or run the image
backend/tests
backend/market_data_demo.py
planning
test
scripts
docs
*.md
!backend/README.md
LICENSE
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
